## Plain-language descriptions of system and network failures, shared
## by the app and every plugin.

io-not-found = The file or folder couldn't be found. It may have been moved or deleted.
io-permission-denied = NotIn Plus doesn't have permission to access this file or folder.
io-storage-full = There isn't enough space on this device. Free up some space and try again.
io-file-too-large = The file is too large.
io-read-only = This location is read-only, so NotIn Plus can't save there.
io-already-exists = Something with that name already exists.
io-timed-out = It took too long to respond. Try again.
io-connection = The connection was lost. Check your network and try again.
io-interrupted = The operation was interrupted. Try again.
io-invalid-data = The file is damaged or isn't in the expected format.
io-unsupported = This isn't supported on this device.
io-busy = The file is in use by another app. Close it and try again.
io-out-of-memory = The device ran out of memory. Close some apps and try again.
io-other = Something went wrong while reading or saving files. Try again.

net-offline = Couldn't connect. Check your internet connection and try again.
net-timed-out = The server took too long to respond. Try again later.
# $status is the HTTP status code, such as 503.
net-server-error = The server had a problem (error { $status }). Try again later.
net-other = The download didn't complete. Check your connection and try again.
